== Notes ==
* The Hot Bombs ({{dlc|r}} and Sad Bombs) he throws are not affected by {{t|Safety Scissors}}.

== Trivia ==
* Big Horn appears to be an adult version of Little Horn.
* Upon defeat, Big Horn frowns and retreats into his hole. He does not explode into blood upon defeat.
** Big Horn's hands also have a death animation, which only plays if Big Horn is killed while they're on-screen. The hands briefly shake and retreat into the holes.
* Big Horn had a [https://twitter.com/tyronerodriguez/status/748593859710509056 teaser on Twitter by Tyrone Rodriguez].
* During the versus screen, Big Horn will growl despite the battle not starting yet. Big Horn is one of seven ({{dlc|r}} 5) bosses that can be heard during the versus screen, the other six ({{dlc|r}} 4) being {{e|The Stain}}, {{e|The Forsaken}}, {{e|Mom}}, {{dlc|nr}} {{e|Mom's Heart}}, {{dlc|nr}} {{e|It Lives!}}, and {{e|Mother}}.
* {{dlc+|r}} Big Horn's hand makes an appearance in the effects of the Item {{i|Little Horn}}. His hand appears grabbing and crushing any [[monster]]s and performing the slap attack on Bosses.
** His hand also appeared from a pit to pull down {{e|Dark Esau}} when he was killed, prior to patch [[v1.7.5]].{{dlc-}}
* Big Horn's unique stun animation might be a reference to Nintendo's ''Punch Out'' series.
* Similar to Little Horn, who was based on the fourth beast's "little horn" from the seventh chapter of the [[wikipedia:Book of Daniel|Book of Daniel]], it is possible that Big Horn is based on the four-horned goat's little horn from the [[wikipedia:Daniel 8|eighth chapter]] of the same book, where it mentions that the horn will grow extraordinarily into a great horn and triggers the apocalypse.
* {{dlc|r}} {{e|Blighted Ovum}}, Big Horn, {{e|Triachnid}}, {{e|Isaac}} and {{e|???}} are the only bosses whose portraits were completely changed in ''Repentance'' (beyond simply adding more detail). Of these, only Triachnid, Isaac, and ??? didn't receive new sprites.

